title: Photo Negative
text: A COMPLEMENTOR lets a beam through but swaps its colour for the opposite one: blue comes out yellow, red comes out cyan. It works on straight beams or on slanted ones, depending on how you turn it.
trick: complementor basics: blue becomes yellow, and the complementor must be turned to suit a diagonal beam
motif: diagonal
expect: recolours>=1
proof: not proved: complementor rules are approximate in clingo; no other solution found
